      "text": "SN1 mechanism: tert-butyl bromide hydrolysis\n\nUnimolecular substitution: the slow ionisation to a tertiary carbocation, then capture by water. Four states with the energy of each.\n\nSN1: tert-butyl bromide hydrolysis: 2 reactant(s) → 2 product(s), 4 states.\nStates: Reactants → Carbocation → Oxonium ion → Products.\nOverall ΔH = -20 kJ/mol; highest transition state 90 kJ/mol above the reactants (the rate-determining step is Reactants → Carbocation).\nThe carbocation is the high-energy intermediate: the first transition state (90 kJ/mol) is the rate-determining step.",
